@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+aster-rtw89 is a Rust port of parts of Linux's rtw89 driver
+(drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89): the power sequences, the eFuse
+layout, the firmware download and its secure-boot keys, the MAC's DMAC and
+CMAC initialization of both generations (mac.c, mac_be.c), the PCIe rings,
+descriptors and interrupts (pci.c, pci_be.c), the H2C commands (fw.c), the
+PHY tables' parser, the channel, TX power, coexistence and calibration code
+of the chips it supports (rtw8852a.c, rtw8852b*.c, rtw8851b.c, rtw8852c.c,
+rtw8922a.c and their _rfk.c, phy.c, phy_be.c, efuse.c, efuse_be.c), and the
+register, bit and calibration-table definitions that src/regs.rs and
+src/rfk_tables.rs hold as generated from Linux's headers and sources.
+Linux licenses those files as "GPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause"; this port takes
+them under BSD-3-Clause. The port's own code is under the MPL-2.0, like the
+rest of this kernel.
